onal, gold, and mortgage and other loans. It also provides various micro, small, and medium enterprises schemes and loans; banking products for government customers; agricultural schemes and loans; corporate banking products and services consist of loans against future lease rentals, working capital financing, and term loans; EXIM finance and cash management services, as well as gold card schemes for exporters; and international banking products and services. In addition, the company offers life and general insurance services; and depository, mutual funds, merchant banking, and application supported by blocked amount services. Further, the company provides mobile and internet banking, SMS banking, missed call, e-statement, ATM, passbook updating machine, and electronic cheque deposit machine services; and point of sale (PoS) is the payment acceptance solutions, NFC-enabled terminals facilitating quick payments, as well as debit and credit cards. Punjab National Bank was incorporated in 1894 and is headquartered in New Delhi, India."}}